          "message": {
            "text": "Authentication forgery family: internal-token HMAC key publicly disclosed, default JWT secret, and query-parameter token acceptance\n\nThe backend's authentication middleware (middleware/auth.ts) can be satisfied by three separately forgeable token classes: (a) JWTs signed with the hard-coded default secret `super-agent-local-dev-secret-change-in-production` that config applies whenever JWT_SECRET is unset in local auth mode; (b) \"internal service tokens\" whose HMAC key in Cognito mode is derived from the Cognito userPoolId — a value the backend itself discloses unauthenticated at GET /api/auth/config; (c) JWTs passed as a `?token=` query parameter on any route, which leak into logs, referrers, and proxy histories. Each allows impersonating any user, role, and organization."
          },
          "locations": [
