        {
          "ruleId": "CWE-798",
          "ruleIndex": 4,
          "level": "error",
          "message": {
            "text": "Hardcoded Redis password and unset deployment secrets (REDIS_PASSWORD/JWT_SECRET) in provisioning scripts\n\nThe infrastructure provisioning sets a hardcoded, repository-published Redis password on the EC2 host Redis, while both deployment env-generation paths emit an empty REDIS_PASSWORD for the backend. The CI env template also omits JWT_SECRET, letting the backend fall back to its hardcoded default signing secret. Together these leave the job-queue/cache layer open to anyone who can reach Redis and leave JWTs forgeable on CI-provisioned deployments."
          },
          "locations": [
            {
              "physicalLocation": {
