              "timestamp": "2026-11-21 10:03:11 UTC",
              "target": "/workspace/agentcore-superagent-update/super-agent (backend)",
              "cwe": "CWE-306",
              "impact": "Unauthenticated cost/DoS: repeated invocation of the (paid) avatar generation service when enabled, billed to the operator. Unauthenticated reads of avatar images by key (tenant/user avatars are generally low-sensitivity) and unauthenticated presigned-URL minting for arbitrary keys within the avatar service's scope, which can also leak the S3 bucket layout. No demonstrated access to non-avatar data.",
              "technical_analysis": "In routes/avatarRoutes.ts, POST /avatars/upload (line 11) and GET /avatars/presign/:key (line 167) include `{ preHandler: [authenticate] }`, but POST /avatars/generate (~line 46), POST /avatars/generate-batch (~line 101), and the catch-all `GET /avatars/*` proxy do not. The generation handler calls avatarService.generateAvatar(prompt) (an external image-generation call) gated only on the ENABLE_AVATAR_GENERATION env flag, not on any identity. The proxy handler strips leading avatars/ prefixes, re-prefixes the key, and streams avatarService.getAvatarData(key) with Cache-Control: public, max-age=86400. Fastify applies only the preHandlers a route declares, so these routes are anonymous.",
              "remediation_steps": "Add `preHandler: [authenticate]` to the generate, generate-batch, presign, and retrieval routes in avatarRoutes.ts (mirroring the upload route in the same file), and add rate limiting on the generation endpoints. For presign/retrieval, restrict acceptable keys to the `avatars/` prefix and validate the key shape before signing.",
              "counterevidence": "Checked: POST /avatars/upload (line 11) and GET /avatars/presign/:key (line 167) DO apply `preHandler: [authenticate]` — the omission on generate/generate-batch/proxy is therefore an inconsistency, not an intentional public design. The generate endpoints are gated by the ENABLE_AVATAR_GENERATION env flag (disabled by default), which reduces exposure of the cost-heavy path but is an operator setting, not a control that ships enforced. The proxy endpoint discloses only objects under the avatars/ prefix. No auth, rate limit, or per-key ACL was found on the cited routes.",
              "confidence": "high",
              "confidence_rationale": "Direct source read of all avatar route registrations confirming the absence of the authenticate preHandler (present on other routes in the same file), plus a local unit PoC (avatar-routes.authz.poc.test.ts) confirming unauthenticated 200 responses. Production exposure and cost per request not measured.",
              "severity_change_conditions": "Measured per-generation cost or confirmation that ENABLE_AVATAR_GENERATION is enabled in production would keep/raise availability impact; evidence that the generation endpoints are disabled everywhere in production would lower this to low.",
              "poc": {
                "description": "1. Send POST /api/avatars/generate with body {\"role\":\"x\"} and no Authorization header — the request is processed and generation is attempted (when ENABLE_AVATAR_GENERATION is on). 2. Send POST /api/avatars/generate-batch with {\"roles\":[\"a\",\"b\",...]} — same. 3. Send GET /api/avatars/<key> unauthenticated — the avatar object is streamed from S3 via the proxy with a public 24h cache header. 4. Control: the same request without a token to /api/avatars/upload or /api/avatars/presign/<key> returns 401, showing those routes do enforce auth.",
                "script_available": true
