                "contextual_cvss_reasoning": "Entry point is the WebSocket upgrade handled by @fastify/websocket registered in backend/src/websocket/execution.gateway.ts:127, which dispatches onto the pinned ws 8.19.0 server. Any network peer able to reach the backend's WS endpoint can send the tiny-fragment stream the advisory describes — no authentication is required before the peer starts sending frames (auth is message-level in the gateway), so privileges_required N and user_interaction N. The sink is ws's per-connection fragment accumulation; the demonstrated impact class is memory exhaustion of the Node process hosting the chat execution gateway, i.e. availability H for that service, with no confidentiality or integrity effect."
