          "ruleId": "CWE-345",
          "ruleIndex": 14,
          "level": "warning",
          "message": {
            "text": "CVE-2026-104850 in @modelcontextprotocol/sdk 1.29.0 (OAuth credential redirection to attacker-chosen MCP server)\n\nThe agentcore runtime pins `@modelcontextprotocol/sdk` 1.29.0 in `agentcore/package-lock.json` (transitive via `@anthropic-ai/claude-agent-sdk` 0.2.141). SDK versions 1.12.0–<1.31.0 are affected by CVE-2026-104850 (advisory CVSS 7.5): the OAuth client support lets the MCP server a client connects to decide which authorization server receives the client's OAuth credentials — stored/pre-provisioned credentials are not bound to their authorization server, so a malicious or compromised MCP server can name its own authorization server in its protected-resource metadata and, without user interaction, receive the client's refresh token."
          },
          "locations": [
            {
              "physicalLocation": {
                "artifactLocation": {
                  "uri": "agentcore/src/agent-runner.ts"
