          "properties": {
            "security-severity": "0.0",
            "strix_vuln_class_hash": "2f4dfd68c026c5eee20037c4db637fd5eac515b45f6e5e91344eb48fb6a29ffe",
            "strix": {
              "id": "vuln-0022",
              "severity": "info",
              "cvss": 0.0,
              "timestamp": "2026-11-21 10:04:30 UTC",
              "target": "super-agent (backend)",
              "cve": "CVE-2026-25223",
              "cwe": "CWE-436",
              "impact": "Any route that relies solely on Fastify's Content-Type-based body validation accepts unvalidated bodies. In this codebase most route handlers additionally validate through zod `schema.parse` at handler level, which limits the demonstrated impact to routes whose validation exists only at the Fastify schema layer; the exact set of such routes was not exhaustively enumerated. The bypass is remotely triggerable by any unauthenticated client on any JSON route.",
              "remediation_steps": "Upgrade fastify to >= 5.7.2 in backend/package.json (e.g. ^5.12.2, which also covers the other 2026 fastify CVEs) and regenerate the lockfile. For the app-hosting/poc services on fastify 4.29.1, upgrade to the fixed 5.x line or accept that the 4.x line no longer receives security patches. Ensure every mutating route enforces a handler-level zod parse so validation does not depend solely on the framework layer.",
              "dependency_metadata": {
                "package_name": "fastify",
                "installed_version": "5.6.2",
                "advisory_cvss": 7.5,
                "package_ecosystem": "npm",
                "manifest_path": "backend/package-lock.json",
                "fixed_version": "5.7.2",
                "reachability": "reachable",
                "reachability_evidence": "Entry point: every HTTP request to the backend API — `backend/src/app.ts:57` creates the Fastify instance (`const app = Fastify({...})`) that serves all routes. Package call: Fastify's content-type-parser selects the validation schema from the request Content-Type header, which the advisory says can be bypassed with a trailing tab; this runs on the attacker's request itself, so the vulnerable code executes for any crafted request (no further call needed). Route schemas using this validation exist (e.g. backend/src/routes/workflows.routes.ts:163, :218, :276, :353 declare `schema:` bodies). The mitigating observation is that routes such as workflows.routes.ts:137 wrap handling in a zod `validateSchema` call independent of Fastify's validation, so not every route's validation is bypassable — but the Fastify-layer bypass itself demonstrably executes. The app-hosting/poc services (app-host-api and runtime) pin fastify 4.29.1 with the same advisory applying (fixed in their line at 5.x per the advisory; 4.x itself is EOL and unpatched).",
                "contextual_cvss_breakdown": {
                  "attack_complexity": "L",
                  "attack_vector": "N",
                  "availability": "N",
                  "confidentiality": "N",
                  "integrity": "N",
                  "privileges_required": "N",
                  "scope": "U",
                  "user_interaction": "N"
                },
                "contextual_cvss_score": 0.0,
                "contextual_cvss_vector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:N/I:N/A:N",
                "contextual_cvss_reasoning": "Fastify 5.6.2 is instantiated as the production API server (backend/src/app.ts:57) and its Content-Type routing runs on every request; routes with JSON body schemas exist (e.g. backend/src/routes/workflows.routes.ts:163,218,276,353). The bypass primitive is therefore exercised by any network client sending a tab-suffixed Content-Type. However, the application's routes overwhelmingly validate bodies a second time through zod schemas at handler level (backend/src/routes/workflows.routes.ts:137 validateSchema calling schema.parse before use), and no route was identified whose entire input-validation guarantee rests on the Fastify JSON-schema layer; without a route whose security depends solely on Fastify body validation, the bypass does not yield a demonstrated confidentiality/integrity effect. The same tab-Content-Type bypass also exists in the app-hosting/poc services pinned to fastify 4.29.1 (app-hosting/poc/services/app-host-api and services/runtime package-lock.json), which are PoC-grade code. Metrics reflect the demonstrated-impact rule: N/N/N with the exposure documented."
              }
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "ruleId": "CWE-20",
          "ruleIndex": 16,
          "level": "note",
          "message": {
            "text": "ip-address 10.2.0 in agentcore (CVE-2026-69192 octal host confusion, not applicable as used)\n\nThe agentcore runtime pins `ip-address` 10.2.0 in `agentcore/package-lock.json` (transitive via `@anthropic-ai/claude-agent-sdk` -> `@modelcontextprotocol/sdk`). Prior to 10.3.1, `Address4` accepts octets with a leading zero and decodes them as decimal, while the network stack (WHATWG URL parser, inet_aton, getaddrinfo) decodes leading-zero octets as octal — the library and the network stack disagree about which host a string names (CVE-2026-69192, advisory CVSS 8.6). Applications that build trust-boundary decisions (e.g. private-IP / SSRF allowlist checks) on Address4.isPrivate() can be tricked into connecting to a different host than the one validated."
          },
          "locations": [
            {
              "physicalLocation": {
                "artifactLocation": {
                  "uri": "agentcore/package-lock.json"
                },
                "region": {
                  "startLine": 1994,
                  "endLine": 1994,
                  "snippet": {
                    "text": "\"node_modules/ip-address\": {"
                  }
                }
              },
              "message": {
                "text": "pins ip-address 10.2.0"
              }
            }
          ],
          "partialFingerprints": {
            "primaryLocationLineHash": "6f66515c723783e9ea0cd5d709cd69556a23d0ad113fcaaa02de066abf8dae27"
          },
          "properties": {
            "security-severity": "0.0",
            "strix_vuln_class_hash": "26bb1280259e707c514bd43346da306b9d78db5f37862e33926ff041abac7427",
            "strix": {
