                "reachability_evidence": "Import check: no application code imports ip-address — a complete search of agentcore/src, backend/src and frontend/src for 'ip-address', 'Address4', 'Address6' finds no imports or symbol usage (the only matches are an unrelated ipAddress field in backend/src/services/webhook.service.ts:140, a plain string compared with Array.includes, not the library). Resolution chain: @anthropic-ai/claude-agent-sdk@0.2.141 -> @modelcontextprotocol/sdk@1.29.0 -> ip-address@10.2.0 (agentcore/package-lock.json:1994). Affected-symbol check: the advisory's vulnerable symbols (new Address4(...), correctForm(), isPrivate()) have no caller in application code, and the webhook allowedIps check at backend/src/services/webhook.service.ts:155 uses exact string matching against request.ip, not the library. Nothing the shipped code loads invokes the library's parsing on attacker-controlled input, so the advisory does not apply to this codebase beyond the pinned-version exposure.",
                "contextual_cvss_breakdown": {
