          "message": {
            "text": "undici 6.24.1 in backend (CVE-2026-109383 dropped TLS callback, not reachable as used)\n\nThe backend pins `undici` 6.24.1 in `backend/package-lock.json` (transitive via `@anthropic-ai/claude-agent-sdk` and `discord.js`). undici versions 4.0.0–<6.29.1 are affected by CVE-2026-109383 (advisory CVSS 9.1): the Agent dispatcher deep-clones its constructor options via JSON before forwarding them to per-origin pools, silently dropping a caller-supplied `tls.checkServerIdentity` callback — so a TLS peer that a custom certificate check was written to reject is silently accepted if it passes Node's default checks."
