          "ruleId": "CWE-95",
          "ruleIndex": 18,
          "level": "error",
          "message": {
            "text": "Authenticated RCE via eval() of workflow custom transform expression\n\nThe workflow execution engine evaluates attacker-supplied transform expressions with JavaScript eval() without any sanitization or sandboxing. An authenticated user with ordinary 'member' role in an organization can supply a workflow whose action node carries a crafted custom transform expression, execute it, and achieve arbitrary code execution in the backend Node.js process."
          },
          "locations": [
            {
              "physicalLocation": {
                "artifactLocation": {
                  "uri": "SECURITY.md"
                }
              }
            },
            {
              "logicalLocations": [
                {
                  "fullyQualifiedName": "super-agent backend (local repository /workspace/agentcore-superagent-update)",
                  "kind": "resource"
                }
              ]
            }
          ],
          "partialFingerprints": {
            "primaryLocationLineHash": "9b4d15aa3dea1333cff82f044b494233b75552707b644535bce0a1ac87760eae"
          },
          "properties": {
            "security-severity": "8.8",
            "strix_vuln_class_hash": "942321e822964e050cb2297103122e6babcb2251d115b4b20f8b2d04d8287dd4",
            "synthetic_location": true,
            "strix": {
              "id": "vuln-0025",
              "severity": "high",
              "cvss": 8.8,
              "timestamp": "2026-11-21 10:06:56 UTC",
              "target": "super-agent backend (local repository /workspace/agentcore-superagent-update)",
              "cwe": "CWE-95",
              "impact": "Full server-side code execution in the backend process: arbitrary file read/write (demonstrated by writing a marker file via fs.writeFileSync), access to the entire process environment (demonstrated by enumerating process.env), and by extension the Postgres/Redis/S3/AWS credentials held by the process. This compromises all tenants' data.",
              "technical_analysis": "`POST /workflows/:workflowId/execute` (backend/src/routes/execution.routes.ts:154) is guarded by `authenticate, requireModifyAccess, enforceTokenQuota`. `requireModifyAccess = requireRole('owner','admin','member')` (backend/src/middleware/auth.ts:280), so any ordinary org member qualifies. The request body's `canvasData.nodes` is validated only as `z.array(z.unknown())` (backend/src/schemas/workflow.schema.ts:48), so node content — including transform configurations — is fully attacker-controlled. During execution the action executor dispatches to `applyCustomTransform` (backend/src/services/node-executors/action-executor.ts:195), which at lines 316-325 substitutes the `data` placeholder and calls `eval(evalExpr)` with the raw attacker-supplied `transformConfig.expression`. There is no allowlist, sandbox, or vm isolation; the code's own comment in the sibling code-artifact executor acknowledges \"In production, use vm2 or isolated-vm\".\n\nScope note on the same class: `applyFilter`/`applyReduce` (lines 265, 290) contain equivalent eval sinks but are unreachable from the dispatch switch. The condition-executor's eval is neutralized by a paren-blocking regex. `code-artifact-executor.ts:296` (`const result = eval(code)`) is a second live sink of the same class, currently blocked only incidentally: a top-level `return` in the generated code throws a SyntaxError before eval. Fixing that functional bug without replacing eval re-opens it; any fix must cover both sinks.",
              "remediation_steps": "Remove eval from the transform pipeline. Replace expression evaluation with a restricted, whitelisted transformation DSL or a sandboxed interpreter (e.g. isolated-vm with no host bindings), and validate transform expressions server-side before persisting or executing them. Apply the same treatment to code-artifact-executor.ts:296, which evals node 'code' fields of the same provenance. Ensure workflow canvas node payloads are structurally validated (schema-restricted), not z.array(z.unknown()).",
              "counterevidence": "Searched for sanitization/containment on the path: nodes are validated only as z.array(z.unknown()) (workflow.schema.ts), and the preHandlers on the execute route are authenticate, requireModifyAccess, enforceTokenQuota — no content filter on node expressions. eval executes in-process, so no vm2/isolated-vm sandbox applies. The only mitigations found are that the attacker must be an authenticated org member with modify access to the workflow, and that sibling paths (applyFilter/applyReduce) happen to be unreachable. No WAF or expression allowlist exists in the code path examined.",
              "confidence": "high",
              "severity_change_conditions": "Confirmation that the workflow execute endpoint is reachable by unauthenticated or self-service-registered users in production would raise severity toward critical; conversely, evidence that transform expressions are filtered by an upstream allowlist not present in this repository would lower it.",
              "poc": {
                "description": "1. Authenticate as any user who is a 'member' (or higher) of an organization.\n2. Create or edit a workflow whose canvasData contains an action node with a transform config of type 'custom' whose expression is crafted JavaScript.\n3. POST /api/workflows/:workflowId/execute with the crafted canvasData.\n4. The engine reaches applyCustomTransform, which evals the expression in-process.\n5. Observe side effects: a marker file written to disk via process.getBuiltinModule('fs').writeFileSync, and Object.keys(process.env).length returned through the node output — arbitrary code execution confirmed.",
                "script_available": true
              }
            }
          }
        },
