            "text": "token storage in localStorage / session handling — No issue identified: frontend browser storage: services/cognito.ts (TOKEN_KEYS localStorage incl. refresh_token), services/auth.ts:50-62, services/api/restClient.ts:26-32,46-58\n\nAll tokens (local JWT, Cognito id/access/refresh tokens) are stored in localStorage, not sessionStorage or HttpOnly cookies — XSS-stealable and the refresh token persists indefinitely (no clearTokens on getIdToken expiry, only on failed refresh). Logout is reasonably complete: AuthContext.logout → cognito logout() clears all 5 keys and redirects to Cognito logout; localLogout clears local token. restClient.setAuthToken also writes 'cognito_id_token' key, mixing modes. This is a hardening/defense-in-depth finding (storage choice amplifies any future XSS; no demonstrated XSS exists — all render paths are escaped). Not a standalone vulnerability."
