          "ruleId": "strix-coverage/cors-wildcard-credentials-true-with-bearer-token-auth-model",
          "ruleIndex": 45,
          "kind": "pass",
          "level": "none",
          "message": {
            "text": "CORS wildcard + credentials:true with Bearer-token auth model — No issue identified: backend CORS config (app.ts:79-100, config/index.ts:64 CORS_ORIGIN default '*')\n\nConfirmed default is origin:true (reflect any origin) + credentials:true when CORS_ORIGIN='*'. However the backend uses no cookies anywhere (auth is Authorization: Bearer JWT; no setCookie in middleware/auth.ts; only logging redaction mentions cookie) — credentialed cross-origin reads therefore cannot attach ambient credentials, and the API requires an explicit Bearer token an attacker's page never possesses. gen-base-env.py does not set CORS_ORIGIN, so the wildcard default ships in deployment, but with token-header auth the impact is limited to unauthenticated/public endpoints (webhook trigger, avatar generate, Swagger) which are same-data regardless of origin. Weak misconfig observation, already folded into the config finding (entry ea19f7); not an independent exploitable vuln."
          },
          "locations": [
            {
              "logicalLocations": [
