            "text": "horizontal IDOR within org (session sharing design intent) — No issue identified: chat.service.ts:126 getSessionById + chat.routes.ts session detail/workspace endpoints\n\nSession detail endpoints (getSessionById) are org-scoped but not user-scoped, and the session LIST endpoint is user-scoped (getSessions → findByUser, chat.service.ts:105-106) — so other users' sessions never appear in a member's UI list; cross-user access is only possible by guessing/enumerating session UUIDs. No code comment documents org-level sharing as intended, but the related KB/file scoping precedent in this codebase is org-level (file.service.ts org-prefix checks), and the Backend AuthZ Agent already filed this org-level scoping family (chat IDOR entry a8217e / vuln reports). No separate exploitable finding beyond what's already reported; reclassify as already-covered design observation rather than a distinct vuln."
