          "ruleId": "strix-coverage/backend-api-key-persistence-across-agentcore-container-invocations",
          "ruleIndex": 47,
          "kind": "open",
          "level": "none",
          "message": {
            "text": "backend API key persistence across AgentCore container invocations — Requires further review: agentcore/src/index.ts:74 process.env.AUTH_TOKEN = payload.backend_api_key\n\nagentcore is a long-lived node http server (src/index.ts:27+): each POST /invocations writes payload.backend_api_key into process.env.AUTH_TOKEN and it is never cleared after the invocation's SSE stream ends. If the AgentCore runtime reuses one container across invocations (its documented execution model), the key from invocation N stays in the env for invocation N+1 — potentially a different tenant's invocation, where workspace files from prior runs could also persist (same code never cleans /workspace between invocations either; restoreWorkspaceFromS3 overwrites but doesn't clear). Cannot determine from the local repo whether AgentCore containers are reused per-tenant or torn down per invocation (platform lifecycle outside this codebase) — open proof gap; even if reused, the values are per-org backend keys within the same deployment, limiting cross-tenant impact. Not reportable without container lifecycle evidence."
          },
          "locations": [
            {
